{"text": "Lesson six, pillar three, compression and the quality budget. Production language models carry more precision than next-token prediction needs, and many weights can be skipped. Compression spends a quality budget to cut capacity, cut bandwidth, and, with the right kernels, raise usable compute. Most of these methods are post-training. You start from a finished checkpoint. Having the bytes per weight halves both the footprint and the traffic during decode. The catch is outliers. A few channels are orders of magnitude larger than the rest, and a naive uniform grid wastes its range on them. Weight-only methods matter 1st, because decode traffic is mostly weights. GPTQ brings second-order error correction down to four bits at huge scale. AWQ protects the channels that activations say are salient. Quip rotates the weights so outliers spread out. Bitnet trains a tiny weight alphabet from scratch. That is training-aware, not a post-training recipe. Activations are harder because they are computed online and they move. SmoothQuant rescales each channel so the difficulty moves from activations onto weights. The production point the survey highlights is 4-bit weights with 8-bit activations, co-designed with the kernel. The cache has its own quantization. KIVI is the one to remember. It is asymmetric and about 2 bits, with no extra tuning. Keys use per-channel quantization, values use per-token quantization, do not swap those. Cache quantization stacks with grouped query attention because they touch different terms of the footprint. Pruning removes structure rather than bits. Unstructured sparsity can zero half the weights, but ordinary hardware cannot accelerate arbitrary zeros. The practical pattern is two of every four weights kept. Sparse tensor cores run that pattern at about twice dense throughput. Distillation builds a smaller student. Training on the teacher's text is mismatched because the student later samples Its own text. On-policy distillation trains on the student's own rollouts. The data distribution matters more than the exact divergence. Deployed models are quantized and pruned and distilled. Memory savings often multiply. Quality errors do not add. Later calibration assume the activations of the model that entered that stage. Change the architecture 1st, and a grid fit to the dense model can collapse.", "language": "en", "duration": 145.008, "words": [{"text": "Lesson", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.42}, {"text": "six,", "start": 0.46, "end": 0.8}, {"text": "pillar", "start": 1.46, "end": 1.741}, {"text": "three,", "start": 1.821, "end": 2.101}, {"text": "compression", "start": 2.601, "end": 3.181}, {"text": "and", "start": 3.321, "end": 3.421}, {"text": "the", "start": 3.421, "end": 3.501}, {"text": "quality", "start": 3.541, "end": 3.941}, {"text": "budget.", "start": 4.021, "end": 4.361}, {"text": "Production", "start": 4.962, "end": 5.402}, {"text": "language", "start": 5.462, "end": 5.822}, {"text": "models", "start": 5.862, "end": 6.202}, {"text": "carry", "start": 6.262, "end": 6.502}, {"text": "more", "start": 6.602, "end": 6.802}, {"text": "precision", "start": 6.862, "end": 7.362}, {"text": "than", "start": 7.422, "end": 7.543}, {"text": "next-token", "start": 7.603, "end": 8.203}, {"text": "prediction", "start": 8.263, "end": 8.703}, {"text": "needs,", "start": 8.763, "end": 9.123}, {"text": "and", "start": 9.563, "end": 9.643}, {"text": "many", "start": 9.703, "end": 9.903}, {"text": "weights", "start": 10.003, "end": 10.263}, {"text": "can", "start": 10.303, "end": 10.423}, {"text": "be", "start": 10.463, "end": 10.524}, {"text": "skipped.", "start": 10.644, "end": 11.004}, {"text": "Compression", "start": 11.604, "end": 12.124}, {"text": "spends", "start": 12.204, "end": 12.484}, {"text": "a", "start": 12.504, "end": 12.524}, {"text": "quality", "start": 12.584, "end": 12.984}, {"text": "budget", "start": 13.064, "end": 13.364}, {"text": "to", "start": 13.424, "end": 13.484}, {"text": "cut", "start": 1